CORE
main.cpp
--cpp11
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ empty pack value stored: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ empty pack sum_of base case: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.3\] line \d+ non-empty pack value stored: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.4\] line \d+ non-empty pack sum_of: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.5\] line \d+ WRONG must FAIL: FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^CONVERSION ERROR$
A variadic constructor with a pack expansion in a function-call-expression
initializer and with two-or-more-element packs.  Exercises two contexts now
handled: the function-call-expression member initializer expands the inner
call-argument pack at its own level rather than duplicating the whole
initializer, and collapses an empty pack to a zero-arg call; and a member
function template's own value parameter pack is expanded in its deferred body,
so the recursive sum_of resolves.  Grounded in N5008 [temp.variadic]/5,7.  The
base-mem-init empty-pack pattern is handled separately and verified by
cpp11_variadic_ctor_pack.
